Andrew wrote:
> [...]

> [...], and now I'm chillin in Minetown (co-aligned priest).  [...]
> [...] Due to an unfortunate mishap
> with hallucination and confusion, the guards are hostile.  Here's
> where the questions start.  I've already killed a couple of them.  How
> much can it hurt me to kill more?  I'm currently piously aligned, and
> I have Orb of Fate as a blessed luckstone now (my old one got
> cursed).  Can I murder without too much fear of repercussions? 

Never observed severe penalties as far as my games evolved. If you've
killed one (instead of fleeing the angered guards, and come back with
a powerful pet to kill them) you can as well kill them all. Then go
kill some more hostile monsters and sacrifice them on your coaligned
altar in minetown.

> Cuz I
> got a cursed mattock but even so they aren't much more than an
> annoyance. 

A mattock is an excellent weapon, but a cursed mattock is very bad
because it's two-handed and severely restricts your actions.

> I dunno if Mjollnir is sufficient to carry me through the
> endgame- so I came up with an idea.

Mjollnir is a bad endgame weapon because of the many shock-resistant
monsters. Ascension is feasible anyway if you don't focus on melee
(which might be hard for a valkyrie and a non-regular player).

> Kill the guard captain, take his
> silver saber, wish for Grayswandir with the castle wand, then
> #twoweapon with them.  Is this feasible? 

Valkyries can get just Basic in sabres, so there are better choices.
I'd also not wish for an artifact but first try to get it as a
sacrifice gift since you've got a coaligned altar available.

(Though, an optional sabre will be helpful on Orcus' level against
the shades later in the game.)

> I've been using mjollnir
> pretty much exclusively since the beginning, so is it now impossible
> to get the needed #enhance points? 

If you're at XL:16 and just enhanced the war hammer to Expert you still
have plenty of room for enhancements. Try to get one of the artifact
brands (or another good artifact longsword) and enhance longswords to
Expert, or first to Skilled and then enhance two-weaponing to Skilled.
For non-melee (ranged) attacks there's the option to throw daggers at
Expert skill. (Given your proficiencies that start with Basic you can
enhance most the above to the maximum values; with an XL:16 available
slots: 15 (minus 6 slots already used for Expert hammer 1+2+3) is 9,
longswords 2, daggers 2+3, two-weaponing 1+2, so you may want to delay
the Expert daggers until you're XL:17.)

> I have a magic marker and a ton of
> blank scrolls- what should I genocide? 

Depends on your skill. Standard choices for advanced players are 'L'
and 'h'.

> Does genociding a class of monsters work in graphics mode? 

The Nethack kernel is the same independent of the user interface. So
yes, class genocide is possible if you read a blessed scroll (and if
you're not confused, which would be fatal).

> I don't want to geno liches and still
> have to deal with demiliches or whatever.  I lack a lot of utility
> stuff- very few good scrolls, couple wands (including a death),

Orcus deep down in Gehennom has a wand of death for you.

> not
> many potions.  Most of my potions went into alchemy a while ago, so
> I'm at 146 HP.  Where can I build up stuff like magic mapping scrolls,

If you haven't found any yet you may want to wish for the first, once
you know them you can write them using a magic marker (worth a wish)
and blank scrolls.

> important healing potions, etc? 

I thought you've already done alchemy? Monsters carry various healing
potions, so try to get them before they quaff them, then do the alchemy
on the stack of potions.

> I have a bunch of spellbooks- is it
> worthwhile to keep and use them or better to sell and try to get more
> protection? 

Getting the nine points of protection from the priest is fine. There's
enough gold for that in Gehennom in case you still lack some coins and
already plundered all the magic memory vaults.

Drop the spellbooks at some stash and get back to your stash when you
want to re-learn the spell (after 19000-20000 turns).

> I don't think there's a Fort Ludios- is there another
> good source of C/K rations somewhere? 

Any barracks and especially the Castle.

> Can I kill a shopkeeper at this point? 

Probably; but it's hard to tell. I usually don't kill them if I want
my items identified by price.

> I've already got a ton of intrinsics: do I need ones like
> disintegration that might not be needed? 

If you have reflection that suffices, but eating the next black dragon
isn't bad either (as long as you're not choking to death).

> How many angels can dance on the head of a pin?

42.

